id: pm-kpftft
title: "Tracker data-quality ratchet in CI: pm validate and pm health run against this repository's own workspace with a shrinking-only per-warning baseline"
description: "CI runs no pm self-check beyond changelog drift, so every tracker data-quality warning class accumulates unenforced and new drift is caught only when a human-initiated review happens to run. Commit a per-warning baseline with owner ids and fail CI when any count regresses, matching the eslint-suppression and import-boundary ratchets already in use for source quality."
type: Task
status: open
priority: 1
tags[4]: ci,governance,quality-gate,validation
created_at: "2026-07-25T18:01:02.045Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-26T17:16:40.450Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 300
acceptance_criteria: "A committed baseline file records the current count for every pm validate warning class plus pm health status, with the owning item id for each entry; a CI gate runs pm validate and pm health against the repository's own workspace using the installed build and fails when any count exceeds its baseline or when health regresses; the baseline is shrinking-only, so an improvement ratchets it down and a regression cannot be absorbed by editing the number upward without an explicit reviewed change; a warning class with no declared owner fails the gate, so unowned drift is a filing gap rather than an accepted state; a newly introduced validator check fails the gate until the baseline is deliberately extended; a negative-control fixture proves the gate fails on a known-bad workspace as pm-k6t4yb requires; the gate runs on the pull-request path within the existing gate time budget"
parent: pm-33cw
risk: low
confidence: high
